=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play firewall/edit-2230 --------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: firewall/edit-2230$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. Port 2230 in hardn's$
# drop-in, sshd not reloaded, so still on 22, ufw inactive. What$
# accepts SSH is not what is configured, so Enable refuses$
# (decision 2; mock stale-listener has what the real plan does).$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured inactive$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
   -  Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] [::]:2230            Not filtered Not bound$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:2230         Not filtered Not bound$
  [ ] [::]:22              Not filtered Not configured$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered Not configured$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  No firewall rules configured$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# sshd isn't listening where its config says, so hardn can't$
# tell which ports SSH uses. Reload sshd or restart ssh.socket,$
# then try again.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured inactive$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
   -  Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] [::]:2230            Not filtered Not bound$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:2230         Not filtered Not bound$
  [ ] [::]:22              Not filtered Not configured$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered Not configured$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  No firewall rules configured$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

